{"id": "EUVD-2026-86749", "enisaUuid": "a318d9ae-11ab-3b15-b1f6-abffe56b6143", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nio_uring/net: don't overconsume buffers when using MSG_TRUNC\n\nWhen a recv/recvmsg is issued with MSG_TRUNC and the incoming packet is\nlarger than the provided buffer, the net layer returns the full length\nof the packet rather than the number of bytes actually copied into the\nbuffer.  As a result, io_uring advances more of the provided buffer ring\nthan was actually filled.  Use the actual filled region size to consume\nthe buffer, but still return the full size to preserve MSG_TRUNC\nsemantics.\n\nTake care with multishot, because that seems to already truncate the\nconsumption based on the available payload size.\n\nThis was reported in https://github.com/axboe/liburing/issues/1619.\n\n[axboe: fold in size_t unsigned fix]", "datePublished": "2026-09-25T10:22:25", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:10:21", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/41d24d2fb168fa05fcaf9ec4e55478411dbbf8e1", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/927d96f91c582b319d104ecf50ec935a8dc29193", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2e70ea75c7bb38a6dc212975f887310f14f7c043", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/6028b543884f8735e057ec9eea4908cd61cab230"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-97618", "GHSA-qrrw-9q98-7ph9"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.2, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "3264ee0d-807e-3f35-aa20-1a209d123d8c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.112"}, {"id": "35da4dae-7dc9-3bcb-b1d4-d3f164276f2c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "ae98dbf43d755b4e111fcd086e53939bef3e9a1a <927d96f91c582b319d104ecf50ec935a8dc29193"}, {"id": "751e7f43-f23a-3d2d-a749-ab51034267f6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "ae98dbf43d755b4e111fcd086e53939bef3e9a1a <2e70ea75c7bb38a6dc212975f887310f14f7c043"}, {"id": "8767f241-f914-3646-86c9-fbeb396aa96d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "959c6649-555b-3a47-b825-735fa9a0d188", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.12"}, {"id": "a6a3ece2-70fe-3504-bd8d-475cf4790c6b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.7"}, {"id": "c019b20f-a856-3f8d-997c-0cc0559ef229", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.53"}, {"id": "c49baa07-c23a-3951-ac82-6899250c71c5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "e7cda97f-9aa9-34db-8c8e-0ce7bf127ea8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "ae98dbf43d755b4e111fcd086e53939bef3e9a1a <6028b543884f8735e057ec9eea4908cd61cab230"}, {"id": "f12bd89b-6338-3d72-b434-f1ad9477e784", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "ae98dbf43d755b4e111fcd086e53939bef3e9a1a <41d24d2fb168fa05fcaf9ec4e55478411dbbf8e1"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "fae59088-1eda-3dc4-b899-08f55c5fed88", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}